Worktree /Users/Apple/Projects/nears-NEARS-1718-chat-order-id-overflow @ d84d464b (clean)

CODE
  UserApp/lib/main.dart:90
      FlutterError.onError = FirebaseCrashlytics.instance.recordFlutterError;
  UserApp/lib/main.dart:81
      final bool collectionEnabled = !kDebugMode;      // => false in a debug build
      await FirebaseCrashlytics.instance.setCrashlyticsCollectionEnabled(collectionEnabled);

  Assigning FlutterError.onError REPLACES the framework default (FlutterError.presentError ->
  dumpErrorToConsole -> debugPrint -> logcat tag "flutter"). The replacement never chains to it.
  With collection disabled in debug, recordFlutterError is a no-op. Net effect: the error is
  reported by the framework and then discarded with no output on any channel.

DIRECT PROOF (not inference) — a RenderFlex overflow that the framework DID report:
  Screen : chat conversation 47, order-card bubble (order 158), locale es, text scale 1.3
  Visual : docs/qa-evidence/NEARS-1718/10-chat-es-scale1.3.png
           - 1164 hazard-stripe px at x[576,597] y[1086,1172]
           - debug overflow label painted, legible: "RIGHT OVERFLOWED BY 1..." (clipped by the
             card's ClipRRect)
           => RenderObject.debugPaintOverflowIndicator ran, i.e. the overflow WAS detected and
              FlutterError.reportError WAS called.
  Logcat : buffer cleared immediately before the capture, then read pid-scoped:
             $ adb -s emulator-5558 logcat -c
             $ adb -s emulator-5558 logcat -d --pid=1702 | grep -c 'RenderFlex overflowed'
             0
             $ adb -s emulator-5558 logcat -d | grep -c 'RenderFlex overflowed'
             0
             $ adb -s emulator-5558 logcat -d | grep -icE 'overflow|EXCEPTION CAUGHT'
             0
           The same window contained 121 live "flutter"-tagged lines from this pid
           (e.g. "I flutter : [NET] endpoint=/api/v1/customer/message/list http_status=200"),
           so the logcat channel itself was healthy — only the framework error was missing.

